        "original_id": "2cb0d674-c21c-51e8-9bd9-718a042afb3b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benjamin Burnley, Yannis Philippakis, Jeremy Hummel, Andrew Mears\n- Bands: Breaking Benjamin, Foals\n- Songs: \"Blow Me Away\", \"Hummer\"\n- Roles: founder, frontman, lead singer, guitarist, vocalist, drummer, record producer\n\nFacts:\n- Benjamin Burnley was born on March 10, 1978, and he is an American musician, composer, and record producer.\n- Benjamin Burnley is best known as the founder and frontman of the American rock band Breaking Benjamin.\n- Yannis Philippakis was born on April 23, 1986, and he is the lead singer and guitarist of the British indie rock band Foals.\n- Benjamin Burnley and then-drummer Jeremy Hummel wrote the song \"Blow Me Away.\"\n- \"Blow Me Away\" was described as featuring hard rock roots, a vocal-centric aesthetic, heavy electric rhythm guitars, and an aggressive male vocalist.\n- \"Hummer\" is the second single by Foals.\n- \"Hummer\" was the first Foals single with Yannis Philippakis on lead vocals, and Andrew Mears was the previous lead vocalist.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
